    "body": "blocked on #715 (UMA, 2026-11-12): the grblHAL post this issue extends (`assets/posts/grblhal.cps`, `grblhal-3axis.mch`, its goldens and `tests/grblhal_post.rs`) is not on upstream main - it exists only in PR #715 (from a contributor's fork, still a draft, labelled `needs-rework`). A PR here cannot use a branch in another fork as its base, so it cannot stack on #715; under AGENTS.md (\"An overlap that can't stack waits for the parent PR to merge\") this issue waits for #715 to merge.\n\nNo code was written; no branch was pushed (local worktree removed). The plan stays as in the claim: first slice = indexing (3+2 on one rotary A along X), with the machine file stating the rotary, `G0 A..` written through a `statesRotary`/`angleWord`-style gate (as fanuc.cps/doosan-dnm.cps do, #1092/#1155), 3-axis moves in the rotated frame from the stream, and simultaneous/wrapped A refused by name (as #785 did for PathPilot) unless grblHAL's public docs state rollover and feed semantics; wrapping then goes to a follow-up and this ships `Refs #714`.\n\nUnblock: when #715 merges, drop `blocked` and pick this again.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
